00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.310
positives and negatives attract.

00:21:08.399 --> 00:21:12.600
So when you have individual water
molecules, they have the opportunity

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:17.129
to interact and essentially bind to
one another and they bind through

00:21:17.129 --> 00:21:18.750
what are called covalent bonds.

00:21:18.899 --> 00:21:24.000
Covalent bonds are relatively weak
bonds, and so as a consequence,

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.459
water can change its confirmation.

00:21:26.939 --> 00:21:32.159
However, covalent bonds are strong enough
that water actually can maintain some

00:21:32.159 --> 00:21:37.139
structure and that structure will vary,
of course, depending on its temperature.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:41.520
So, what you need to know about
water is that indeed it consists

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:45.120
of lots of individual H₂O , and
those H₂O  can arrange themselves in

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:48.720
different ways, and that temperature
is a strong determinant of the

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.730
arrangement of those water molecules.

00:21:50.879 --> 00:21:52.649
That is, they're bonding to one another.

