However, in researching tap water for
this episode by way of looking at the

01:30:03.840 --> 01:30:08.880
peer reviewed research, meta-analysis
reviews, specific research articles where

01:30:08.880 --> 01:30:13.980
specific hypotheses were tested, and in
talking with experts in toxicology and so

01:30:13.980 --> 01:30:16.770
on, it's a pretty grim picture frankly.

01:30:17.040 --> 01:30:23.190
When one looks at what's contained in
most tap water and whether or not the

01:30:23.780 --> 01:30:27.389
compounds that are contained in tap water
are present in sufficient concentrations

01:30:27.540 --> 01:30:29.070
to negatively impact our health.

01:30:29.670 --> 01:30:35.430
And the bad news is that much, if not
all, tap water, believe it or not much if

01:30:35.430 --> 01:30:40.170
not all, tap water contains things that
are bad for the biology of our cells.

01:30:40.320 --> 01:30:43.830
There is a silver lining, however, and
the silver lining is that very simple

01:30:43.860 --> 01:30:49.320
steps that are very inexpensive can
be used to adjust that tap water to

01:30:49.320 --> 01:30:53.040
make it not just safe to drink, but
that makes it perfectly fine to drink.

01:30:53.045 --> 01:30:54.700
So that's the good news, and
we'll get to that in a moment.

01:30:55.559 --> 01:30:59.519
If you are somebody who is interested
in whether or not tap water contains

01:30:59.519 --> 01:31:02.820
things like endocrine disruptors, hormone
disruptors that can negatively impact

01:31:02.820 --> 01:31:07.440
reproductive health in males or females,
or both, there is a wonderful review,

01:31:07.559 --> 01:31:09.030
wonderful, because it's so thorough.

01:31:10.080 --> 01:31:13.650
Although the news isn't great, it's
very thorough, which is great, which is

01:31:13.650 --> 01:31:16.889
entitled Endocrine Disruptors in Water and
Their Effects on the Reproductive System.

01:31:16.889 --> 01:31:22.080
This is a review from 2020 that analyzes
water from a bunch of different sources

01:31:22.080 --> 01:31:27.690
within the world and essentially
focuses on a few key components.

01:31:28.335 --> 01:31:30.975
First of all, it focuses on
the concentration of minerals.

01:31:30.975 --> 01:31:33.015
That is magnesium and
calcium within water.

01:31:33.015 --> 01:31:34.965
Many people don't realize
this, but so-called hard

01:31:34.965 --> 01:31:36.975
water sounds terrible, right?

01:31:36.975 --> 01:31:40.305
But hard water is water that
contains magnesium and calcium,

01:31:40.305 --> 01:31:41.775
which turns out to be a good thing.

01:31:42.705 --> 01:31:44.805
Some water contains more
magnesium and calcium.

01:31:45.195 --> 01:31:46.845
Other water contains less.

01:31:46.875 --> 01:31:50.085
They looked at the presence of
magnesium and calcium because that

01:31:50.085 --> 01:31:52.515
is going to impact the pH of water.

01:31:52.545 --> 01:31:56.265
In general, the higher concentrations
of magnesium and calcium and water, the

01:31:56.269 --> 01:32:00.765
higher the pH that is, the more alkaline
that water is, and the lower levels of

01:32:00.769 --> 01:32:05.144
magnesium and calcium, the more acidic
or lower pH that water tends to be.

01:32:06.135 --> 01:32:11.144
The other thing that this review addresses
is the concentration of so-called

01:32:11.144 --> 01:32:15.225
DBPs: dog bulldog, porcupines, DBPs.

01:32:16.110 --> 01:32:19.500
Which are disinfection
byproducts contained in water.

01:32:19.800 --> 01:32:23.280
So obviously local governments,
the government wants your

01:32:23.340 --> 01:32:24.750
drinking water to be clean.

01:32:24.780 --> 01:32:27.690
They don't want contaminants in,
they don't want sewage in that water.

01:32:28.139 --> 01:32:31.650
They don't want chemical contaminants
that are going to make people

01:32:31.650 --> 01:32:33.630
immediately sick, so they treat water.

01:32:33.630 --> 01:32:37.920
Water treatment plants, treat water
with disinfection products, and those

01:32:37.920 --> 01:32:41.550
disinfection products create things
called disinfection byproducts.

01:32:41.610 --> 01:32:46.500
And the presence of those DBPs
or disinfectant byproducts can

01:32:46.530 --> 01:32:50.940
strongly impact the pH of water by
way of changing the concentrations

01:32:50.940 --> 01:32:52.290
of magnesium and calcium.

01:32:52.469 --> 01:32:55.650
Put differently, I do believe that
governments are trying to provide

01:32:55.650 --> 01:32:59.820
people with clean water, but in doing
so, oftentimes we'll introduce things

01:32:59.820 --> 01:33:02.219
to that water that are not good for us.

01:33:02.309 --> 01:33:06.929
Now, it's very clear that DBPs can
cause endocrine disruption in ways that

01:33:06.929 --> 01:33:08.400
are not good for reproductive health.

01:33:08.400 --> 01:33:12.870
I did a very long, in fact, 4 and a half
hour episode on fertility and vitality.

01:33:13.380 --> 01:33:15.570
That was male and female
fertility, by the way.

01:33:15.919 --> 01:33:20.009
And vitality that again, you can find
at hubermanlab.com that talks about

01:33:20.009 --> 01:33:23.400
all the biological processes involved
in the generation of healthy eggs and

01:33:23.400 --> 01:33:28.320
sperm and, and creating healthy embryos,
implantation embryos, and so forth.

01:33:29.009 --> 01:33:33.900
It's very clear that DBPs have been
shown to disrupt ovarian function,

01:33:33.900 --> 01:33:36.070
spermatogenesis and fertility outcomes.

01:33:36.790 --> 01:33:40.395
Even at concentrations of DBPs
that are present in drinking

01:33:40.395 --> 01:33:42.105
water that comes from the tap.

01:33:42.105 --> 01:33:44.145
Now, does that mean that you
shouldn't drink tap water?

01:33:44.175 --> 01:33:47.105
Well, the answer to that is it depends.

01:33:47.325 --> 01:33:48.405
What does it depend on?

01:33:48.525 --> 01:33:49.665
Well, it depends on several things.

01:33:49.665 --> 01:33:54.825
First of all, I highly recommend
to everybody go online and put

01:33:54.830 --> 01:33:59.265
in your zip code and ask for a
water analysis of water that comes

01:33:59.265 --> 01:34:01.215
out of the tap in that zip code.

