between 200 and $500.

01:41:33.754 --> 01:41:37.485
Probably one of the more common
ones or popular ones is a

01:41:37.485 --> 01:41:39.344
so-called Berkey filter system.

01:41:39.525 --> 01:41:41.955
These are filter systems that, again,
remove the things that you want

01:41:41.960 --> 01:41:44.804
removed from your tap water, and
they can do it at higher volumes.

01:41:44.804 --> 01:41:46.585
And they're typically countertop units.

01:41:47.005 --> 01:41:52.035
They don't require any plugin typically,
or they only require brief plugin

01:41:52.035 --> 01:41:56.054
and electricity, and they're going to
filter out many, many liters or tens of

01:41:56.054 --> 01:41:59.400
liters of water so that you can always
have access to that clean filtered

01:41:59.415 --> 01:42:02.894
water time or day or night without
having to pour over into the pitcher.

01:42:03.165 --> 01:42:06.495
So I mentioned these different options
because again, I realize that people have

01:42:06.495 --> 01:42:08.085
different levels of disposable income.

01:42:08.625 --> 01:42:15.105
As far as I know, there's no tablet or
simple mechanism that can be purchased

01:42:15.105 --> 01:42:19.514
as a transportable, you know pill
that you can just simply throw in

01:42:19.519 --> 01:42:20.924
water and remove the contaminants.

01:42:20.924 --> 01:42:24.644
If anyone is aware of one that
can adequately remove fluoride and

01:42:24.644 --> 01:42:28.005
other contaminants, please put in
the comment section on YouTube.

01:42:28.005 --> 01:42:28.954
That'd be the best place.

01:42:29.264 --> 01:42:32.325
So that I and everyone else can see
it, but hopefully the mention of the

01:42:32.325 --> 01:42:36.269
different filtration systems that I
mentioned  we'll give you some choices

01:42:36.269 --> 01:42:40.200
that I would hope would fall within the
range that one could potentially afford.

01:42:40.530 --> 01:42:42.000
An important note about filtration.

01:42:43.020 --> 01:42:48.300
Just as in our body, there are mechanisms
to signal mechanical changes and

01:42:48.300 --> 01:42:51.750
chemical changes that occur in our
gut, in our brain, etc., elsewhere

01:42:51.780 --> 01:42:55.860
and in general, both mechanical and
chemical changes are signaled across

01:42:55.860 --> 01:42:59.700
the body to invoke different changes,
whether or not those are, you know,

01:42:59.700 --> 01:43:02.940
a response of the immune system or to
make us more alert or more asleep, etc.

01:43:03.600 --> 01:43:09.300
So too filtration capitalizes on
mechanical and chemical filtration.

01:43:09.450 --> 01:43:12.870
What I mean by that is when you
run a fluid water or any other

01:43:12.870 --> 01:43:16.470
fluid through a filter, those
filters are doing two things.

01:43:16.710 --> 01:43:21.720
They are physically constraining which
molecules can go through by creating

01:43:22.080 --> 01:43:27.600
portals, pores that allow certain size
molecules to go through and not others.

01:43:27.690 --> 01:43:32.490
And almost always, they contain
certain chemicals themselves, right?

01:43:32.550 --> 01:43:34.530
Those filters have been treated
with certain chemicals that

01:43:34.530 --> 01:43:37.570
neutralize certain other chemicals.

01:43:37.575 --> 01:43:37.710
Okay?

01:43:37.710 --> 01:43:40.680
So you may be wondering how
when you filter water, you know,

01:43:40.950 --> 01:43:43.350
magnesium and calcium could get
through, but fluoride doesn't.

01:43:43.500 --> 01:43:46.450
And that's because these filters
have been very cleverly designed

01:43:46.710 --> 01:43:52.560
in order to neutralize fluoride or
to prevent large molecules, such as

01:43:52.560 --> 01:43:55.650
sediment and dirt, which is kind of
easy to imagine being filtered, but

01:43:55.655 --> 01:44:00.945
also to allow certain small molecule,
like calcium, which is small-ish, or

01:44:00.945 --> 01:44:04.304
magnesium, which is small-ish to still
pass through into our drinking water.

01:44:04.425 --> 01:44:06.735
And this is wonderful because what
it means is that by filtering our

01:44:06.735 --> 01:44:09.705
water, using any of the methods that
we talked about before, you're still

01:44:09.705 --> 01:44:13.695
going to get whatever magnesium and
calcium was present in that water while

01:44:13.934 --> 01:44:18.255
still adequately removing the fluoride
and other disinfectant byproducts.

01:44:18.434 --> 01:44:20.445
Now, what if you can't
afford any of those options?

01:44:20.474 --> 01:44:23.775
Okay, well here you have an
interesting zero cost option.

01:44:23.775 --> 01:44:27.375
It's not as good as the other ones
of filtering that water, but it is an

01:44:27.380 --> 01:44:30.585
option, and I do think it's important
to give options to people who don't have

01:44:30.590 --> 01:44:35.445
any disposable income for the purpose
of filtering their water, which is to

01:44:35.450 --> 01:44:42.134
draw a gallon or 5 gallons or maybe even
more, tap water out of the tap and put it

01:44:42.134 --> 01:44:45.525
into some, some container, some vessel.

01:44:45.525 --> 01:44:48.045
So it could be one gallon, 5
gallon, 10 gallon container.

01:44:48.195 --> 01:44:52.995
And then to let that tap water sit for
some period of time to allow some of

01:44:52.995 --> 01:44:55.335
the sediment to drop to the bottom.

01:44:55.335 --> 01:44:57.514
Now you might say, well, there's no
sediment, there's nothing contained

01:44:57.514 --> 01:45:01.365
in that tap water and it isn't
fluoride diluted in the water.

01:45:01.365 --> 01:45:02.804
And indeed the answer to that is yes.

01:45:02.804 --> 01:45:06.825
However, there is some evidence that
letting tap water sit out at room

01:45:06.825 --> 01:45:11.085
temperature and outside the pipes that
deliver that water can help remove some,

01:45:11.085 --> 01:45:13.184
not all of the contaminants in that water.

01:45:14.160 --> 01:45:17.040
If, however you are filtering the
water using any of the methods

01:45:17.040 --> 01:45:20.640
that I talked about a few moments
ago, you do not need to do this.

01:45:20.790 --> 01:45:21.000
Okay?

01:45:21.000 --> 01:45:24.090
I realize there's a whole world out there
of people who insist on putting their

01:45:24.090 --> 01:45:27.480
water in the sun or only keeping it in
certain containers and putting it out

01:45:27.480 --> 01:45:29.040
for a few days before they get ingested.

01:45:29.310 --> 01:45:30.660
That to me, seems a bit extreme.

01:45:30.690 --> 01:45:33.690
If you wanna do that, be my guest, but I
don't think most people need to do that.

01:45:33.690 --> 01:45:38.460
However, I do believe that for people who
have zero disposable income to devote to

01:45:38.580 --> 01:45:42.030
paying for any kind of filtration system
for their tap water, they're taking that

01:45:42.120 --> 01:45:46.320
tap water and putting into some container
at room temperature and keeping it room

01:45:46.320 --> 01:45:53.070
temperature for a half day or a day
or more, and then pouring off the top

01:45:53.100 --> 01:45:56.940
two thirds of that water into another
container and consuming the water from

01:45:56.940 --> 01:46:01.170
that second container is going to remove
some, not all of the contaminants that

01:46:01.170 --> 01:46:02.460
one would need to be concerned about.

01:46:02.640 --> 01:46:05.520
And here I should mention something that
I neglected to mention a few moments ago.

01:46:05.700 --> 01:46:09.960
If you were going to do this
zero cost option and, and let the

01:46:09.960 --> 01:46:13.080
water sit out for a bit, you would
want that water to sit uncapped.

01:46:13.140 --> 01:46:14.850
Sorry, I should have
mentioned that before.

01:46:14.910 --> 01:46:18.990
Uncapped, of course, trying to keep
things from falling into that water.

01:46:18.990 --> 01:46:23.040
In fact, you could even put a a little
bit of cloth above it, so you don't

01:46:23.045 --> 01:46:25.500
want things falling into that water,
but you want certain things to be able

01:46:25.500 --> 01:46:29.070
to evaporate off, and you also want
some of the sediment to drop down.

01:46:29.130 --> 01:46:35.070
And the reason why this process of letting
water sit out would work at all is because

01:46:35.519 --> 01:46:38.700
many of the contaminants contained within
water are not present because of the

01:46:38.700 --> 01:46:42.900
source of that water or even the treatment
of that water, but rather because of the

01:46:42.900 --> 01:46:48.690
pipes that that water arrives to your
glass or your, the pot that you have from.

01:46:49.170 --> 01:46:49.320
Okay?

01:46:49.320 --> 01:46:52.650
And here again, there is an
infinite number of variables.

01:46:52.655 --> 01:46:54.990
So some people are living in
buildings for which the pipes are

01:46:54.990 --> 01:46:57.630
very, very old, but very, very clean.

01:46:57.720 --> 01:47:01.290
Believe it or not, some people are
living in newer buildings and structures.

01:47:01.410 --> 01:47:05.910
They have new pipes, but for which the
seals between those pipes contain things

01:47:05.910 --> 01:47:07.559
that are not good for you to consume.

01:47:07.980 --> 01:47:12.540
So by letting water sit out for a while,
you are able to remove some of the

01:47:12.559 --> 01:47:17.010
contaminants present within the pipes of
your home and the building and even the

01:47:17.010 --> 01:47:18.960
pipes that lead to your home or apartment.

01:47:19.350 --> 01:47:22.560
Now, some people get really obsessed
with this old tap water thing and really

01:47:22.560 --> 01:47:26.910
wanna find out all the details about the
pipes and what sorts of, you know, hard

01:47:26.910 --> 01:47:30.150
metals and how much magnesium and how
much calcium are present in their water.

01:47:30.450 --> 01:47:33.150
There are ways that you can test your
drinking water for those sorts of things.

01:47:33.270 --> 01:47:36.435
Most people, I realize, including
myself, are simply not going to do that.

01:47:37.135 --> 01:47:41.220
If you want to know what I do, I tend
to drink water that is filtered through

01:47:41.220 --> 01:47:42.750
one of these lower cost filters.

01:47:43.110 --> 01:47:46.990
Or if I'm going to be consuming a lot
of fluid, I will drink certain kinds

01:47:47.010 --> 01:47:51.000
of fluid that later I'll tell you, I've
been doing an experiment for sake of this

01:47:51.000 --> 01:47:54.990
episode looking at so-called molecular
hydrogen water, which sounds very fancy

01:47:54.990 --> 01:47:57.690
and esoteric and almost a little wacky.

01:47:57.690 --> 01:48:00.510
But it turns out has largely to do
with the amount of magnesium and

01:48:00.510 --> 01:48:02.070
calcium and the pH of that water.

01:48:02.220 --> 01:48:05.220
So if you are somebody who has a very
low budget or simply just wants to

01:48:05.220 --> 01:48:08.850
spend a very small amount of money and
try and still drink tap water, there

01:48:08.850 --> 01:48:11.010
is absolutely a way to do that safely.

01:48:11.010 --> 01:48:13.080
But it does require a few of these steps.

01:48:13.530 --> 01:48:18.240
So, on the topic of magnesium and
calcium, this relates, as I mentioned

01:48:18.245 --> 01:48:20.684
earlier, to the "hardness" of water.

01:48:21.300 --> 01:48:25.290
So what of the hardness of water, you
know, is it better to have more magnesium

01:48:25.290 --> 01:48:26.970
and calcium in your water or less?

01:48:27.945 --> 01:48:30.225
Some people don't like
the taste of hard water.

01:48:30.435 --> 01:48:34.515
They prefer the taste of water
that has less magnesium in calcium.

01:48:34.515 --> 01:48:37.905
However, there I would encourage
you to take a step back and

01:48:37.910 --> 01:48:39.215
consider some of the literature.

01:48:39.305 --> 01:48:43.815
In fact I'll mention a paper in particular
now, published in 2019, which describes

01:48:43.815 --> 01:48:47.325
the quote, regulations for calcium,
magnesium, or hardness in drinking water

01:48:47.325 --> 01:48:49.245
in the European Union member states.

01:48:49.335 --> 01:48:53.235
Turns out in Europe, they do very
detailed  water analysis and that's

01:48:53.235 --> 01:48:56.565
present in a number of really high
quality scientific publications.

01:48:56.775 --> 01:49:01.305
This was a paper published in regulatory
toxicology and pharmacology, and they

01:49:01.515 --> 01:49:04.695
cite a number of different references
in the introduction that, for instance,

01:49:04.695 --> 01:49:09.315
in here I'm quoting statistically
significant inverse association between

01:49:09.315 --> 01:49:11.685
magnesium and cardiovascular mortality.

01:49:11.805 --> 01:49:16.275
Now, again, that's a, an association,
this is not causal, but higher magnesium

01:49:16.280 --> 01:49:19.785
in water, lower cardiovascular mortality.

01:49:20.925 --> 01:49:24.555
They go on to say the highest exposure
category, which are people consuming

01:49:24.555 --> 01:49:29.565
drinking water with magnesium contents
of 8.3 to 19.4 milligrams per liter.

01:49:29.565 --> 01:49:32.895
Again, when you get your water analysis,
you can compare against some of these

01:49:32.895 --> 01:49:36.945
values was significantly associated with
decreased likelihood of cardiovascular

01:49:37.135 --> 01:49:41.745
mortality by 25% compared with
people consuming magnesium content

01:49:41.805 --> 01:49:45.915
of 2.5 to 8.2 milligrams per liter.

01:49:46.335 --> 01:49:49.665
Okay, so what this basically shows,
and, and by the way, the reference

01:49:49.665 --> 01:49:52.300
to that I'll also provide a link
to, in the show note caption.

01:49:52.640 --> 01:49:56.940
What this basically states is that
higher magnesium containing water,

01:49:57.210 --> 01:50:00.210
and it turns out higher magnesium and
calcium  containing water, so-called

01:50:00.240 --> 01:50:04.770
harder water may not taste as good to
you, but turns out to be better for you.

01:50:04.770 --> 01:50:06.810
Now, whether or not it can prevent
you from getting cardiovascular

01:50:06.810 --> 01:50:08.220
disease, I don't know.

01:50:08.250 --> 01:50:12.300
In fact, I would probably just
state no, it probably won't prevent

01:50:12.300 --> 01:50:13.650
you from cardiovascular disease.

01:50:13.650 --> 01:50:15.720
You still need to do all the other
things that are important for

01:50:15.720 --> 01:50:19.135
avoiding cardiovascular disease
and cerebral vascular disease.

01:50:19.785 --> 01:50:23.880
For that and what to do in order
to avoid cardiovascular disease.

01:50:23.880 --> 01:50:26.385
I strongly encourage you to
listen to the episode with Dr.

01:50:26.385 --> 01:50:29.550
Peter Attia, that's coming out in a
few weeks that gets deep into that

01:50:29.550 --> 01:50:32.880
topic and the actionable items for
avoiding cardiovascular disease.

01:50:33.510 --> 01:50:38.250
But basically, as this study quotes,
there is a growing consensus among

01:50:38.280 --> 01:50:42.090
epidemiologists and epidemiological
evidence along with clinical and

01:50:42.090 --> 01:50:45.900
nutritional evidence that's strong
enough to suggest that new guidance

01:50:45.905 --> 01:50:50.220
should be issued in terms of how these
different sources of tap water should

01:50:50.280 --> 01:50:54.240
enhance, not deplete the amount of
magnesium and calcium in that water.

01:50:54.630 --> 01:50:58.200
Now, this ought to raise a very
important question in all of your

01:50:58.205 --> 01:51:01.410
minds, which is why is it that
magnesium and calcium concentrations

01:51:01.415 --> 01:51:03.510
are relevant to cardiovascular disease?

01:51:03.510 --> 01:51:07.410
Is it something about what magnesium does
in cells or what calcium does in cells?

01:51:07.410 --> 01:51:09.150
Are we all magnesium
and calcium deficient?

01:51:09.570 --> 01:51:11.040
Well, it turns out that's not the case.

01:51:11.610 --> 01:51:18.720
The major effect by which magnesium and
calcium in water are likely to impact

01:51:18.724 --> 01:51:21.850
things like blood pressure, cardiovascular
disease, and other aspects of cellular

01:51:21.900 --> 01:51:25.769
function turn out to be somewhat cryptic.

01:51:26.130 --> 01:51:30.690
But we can make that cryptic aspect
very clear by saying that when we

01:51:30.690 --> 01:51:34.650
have more magnesium in particular,
but also calcium present in our water,

01:51:34.650 --> 01:51:39.510
so-called hard water, you increase
the amount of hydrogen in that water.

01:51:39.510 --> 01:51:44.190
It becomes what we call hydrogen rich
and the pH of that water is increased.

01:51:44.490 --> 01:51:49.110
Now again, this does not mean that we are
trying to change the pH of the cells of

01:51:49.115 --> 01:51:51.269
our body in any kind of meaningful way.

01:51:51.269 --> 01:51:52.470
In fact, we don't want to do that.

01:51:52.470 --> 01:51:56.309
We want the pH of the cells of our
body to stay in particular ranges as

01:51:56.309 --> 01:52:01.139
I mentioned earlier, but having more
magnesium and more calcium in our water

01:52:01.500 --> 01:52:04.769
that is increasing the hardness of our
water changes the pH of that water.

01:52:04.769 --> 01:52:11.370
And it turns out that the elevated pH
of water, that is pH of water that tends

01:52:11.370 --> 01:52:13.980
to be somewhere between high sevens.

01:52:14.040 --> 01:52:22.679
So we could say 7.9 up to even 9 or 9.2
is going to be more readily absorbed and

01:52:22.679 --> 01:52:28.320
is going to more favorably impact the
function of our cells than lower pH water.

01:52:28.620 --> 01:52:32.219
Again, I wanna restate this because
I'm a little bit concerned that

01:52:32.219 --> 01:52:35.049
maybe a clip of this is gonna be
taken and, and send elsewhere.

01:52:35.049 --> 01:52:38.130
And someone will get the impression
that I'm saying that we actually want

01:52:38.130 --> 01:52:41.639
to drink high pH water, that we all
need to buy expensive high pH water.

01:52:41.639 --> 01:52:42.809
Turns out that's not the case.

01:52:43.590 --> 01:52:49.620
If you are consuming tap water from a
location where levels of a magnesium are

01:52:49.650 --> 01:52:54.090
sufficiently high in that tap water again,
where the level of magnesium is 8.3 to

01:52:54.519 --> 01:52:59.250
19.4 milligrams per liter of water, that
is, if the water coming out of your tap

01:52:59.250 --> 01:53:04.350
is hard enough, well then chances are you
don't need to enhance the pH of that water

01:53:04.350 --> 01:53:06.000
or change its magnesium concentration.

01:53:06.030 --> 01:53:09.390
If, however, the water that you're
drinking from the tap filtered or

01:53:09.394 --> 01:53:17.700
not, I would hope filtered contains
less than 8.3 milligrams per liter of

01:53:17.705 --> 01:53:22.710
magnesium, well then chances are the
pH of that water is going to be low

01:53:22.710 --> 01:53:27.480
enough that it's not going to be lending
itself to some of the favorable health

01:53:28.080 --> 01:53:30.300
components that higher pH water can.

01:53:30.450 --> 01:53:35.850
Notice, I did not say that lower pH
aka more acidic water is bad for you.

01:53:35.940 --> 01:53:36.870
I didn't say that.

01:53:37.110 --> 01:53:40.500
I said that higher pH
water can be good for you.

01:53:40.710 --> 01:53:43.800
So let's talk about how and why
higher pH water can be good for you.

01:53:43.860 --> 01:53:47.880
And some of the best, and in fact,
very inexpensive sources of higher

01:53:47.880 --> 01:53:52.590
pH magnesium enhanced or simply
tap water that contains sufficient

01:53:52.595 --> 01:53:54.930
magnesium can be used and accessed.

01:53:55.335 --> 01:53:59.385
Many of you are probably wondering whether
or not you can simply boil your tap water

01:53:59.385 --> 01:54:02.625
and thereby decontaminate the tap water.

01:54:03.105 --> 01:54:05.535
There I want to caution you,
it turns out that some of the

01:54:05.535 --> 01:54:09.285
contaminants present in water are
actually made worse by heating water.

01:54:09.765 --> 01:54:14.145
And again, I don't want to open up you
know, a whole catalog of different fears.

01:54:14.675 --> 01:54:19.655
I, like all of you, I presume, use
water to cook pasta, rice, because I'm

01:54:19.660 --> 01:54:21.205
an omnivore, I do consume those things.

01:54:21.575 --> 01:54:26.165
I confess if I make Yerba Matte or any
kind of tea or coffee, I tend to use

01:54:26.435 --> 01:54:31.475
a higher quality water source than tap
water, even if that tap water is filtered,

01:54:31.475 --> 01:54:36.185
because I like the taste far more if I use
a really good source of water, and again,

01:54:36.245 --> 01:54:39.695
because I'm not consuming those beverages
in enormous volumes, that becomes a,

01:54:40.055 --> 01:54:41.795
a relatively inexpensive endeavor.

01:54:42.185 --> 01:54:47.255
But I would caution people against
using boiling or heating of water

01:54:47.255 --> 01:54:51.635
as the only method to decontaminate
their tap water and instead to

01:54:51.695 --> 01:54:54.605
also rely on some of the filtration
systems that I talked about before.

01:54:54.995 --> 01:54:58.595
And as long as we're talking about
the temperature of water, there is

01:54:58.595 --> 01:55:00.935
sort of an ongoing debate online.

01:55:01.235 --> 01:55:03.875
It's not a huge debate, but a number
of people engaged in this debate as

01:55:03.875 --> 01:55:07.895
to whether or not drinking really
cold water or room temperature water

01:55:07.895 --> 01:55:09.695
is better for you or worse for you.

01:55:10.295 --> 01:55:12.005
This is a tough one to resolve.

01:55:12.635 --> 01:55:17.585
It turns out that if water is very, very
cold, that is if you drink it and you can

01:55:17.765 --> 01:55:22.265
feel that cold water making its way down
to your gut and you can actually feel it

01:55:22.265 --> 01:55:27.305
as cold within your gut, that's sort of a,
a you know, back of the envelope, , or I

01:55:27.310 --> 01:55:32.285
should say direct within the gut measure
of cold versus body temperature water,

01:55:33.095 --> 01:55:35.375
that it is going to be slower to absorb.

01:55:35.555 --> 01:55:38.495
That is you're gonna feel it sloshing
around in your stomach for a bit

01:55:38.495 --> 01:55:41.945
longer than if you were to consume
water that is slightly warmer.

01:55:42.584 --> 01:55:45.825
Now, that is not to say that
you should ingest warm water

01:55:45.825 --> 01:55:47.174
or room temperature water.

01:55:47.504 --> 01:55:52.424
However, many people find that when
they drink very cold water or ice water,

01:55:52.754 --> 01:55:57.945
that indeed it can alter the kind of
sensation of the lining of their stomach

01:55:58.065 --> 01:56:01.695
in ways that at least to them feel
like it's altering their digestion.

01:56:01.724 --> 01:56:02.474
And that makes sense.

01:56:02.474 --> 01:56:05.355
The cells that line the gut
are very temperature sensitive.

01:56:05.384 --> 01:56:09.945
You want this so for a number of
reasons, including not consuming

01:56:09.945 --> 01:56:13.094
food that is excessively hot
or cold or damaging your gut.

01:56:13.754 --> 01:56:17.565
But in general, most people know
the temperature of fluid that

01:56:17.570 --> 01:56:19.964
they want to ingest and ingest
that temperature of fluid.

01:56:19.964 --> 01:56:24.014
So most people, for instance, on a
cold day, want a warmer or hot fluid.

01:56:24.044 --> 01:56:26.384
Does that mean that you're not going
to absorb that warmer hot fluid?

01:56:26.415 --> 01:56:27.644
No, of course it doesn't.

01:56:27.644 --> 01:56:29.924
You're going to absorb that
fluid one way or the other.

01:56:29.985 --> 01:56:33.165
So drink fluids at the temperatures
that are to your liking in that moment.

01:56:33.285 --> 01:56:36.075
In other words, what you desire in
that moment and don't worry so much

01:56:36.254 --> 01:56:39.915
about trying to avoid cold beverages
or trying to make sure that you're

01:56:39.915 --> 01:56:43.035
always consuming room temperature
water as opposed to cold water.

01:56:43.065 --> 01:56:46.844
So now with your understanding of
hard water, soft water, magnesium, the

01:56:46.844 --> 01:56:49.964
relationship between magnesium, calcium,
and the pH of water, and remember our

01:56:49.964 --> 01:56:55.115
earlier conversation where we talked
about how higher pH water is actually

01:56:55.120 --> 01:56:59.895
going to move out of the gut and into
the body a bit more readily, and across

01:56:59.895 --> 01:57:03.855
those aquaporin channels more readily
than lower pH, more acidic water.

01:57:04.155 --> 01:57:06.555
Well, that raises the question of
whether or not all these different forms

01:57:06.555 --> 01:57:10.785
of water that are out there, reverse
osmosis water, distilled water, double

01:57:10.785 --> 01:57:16.395
distilled water deuterium-depleted
water, alkaline water, as it's often

01:57:16.395 --> 01:57:21.915
called, whether or not any or all of
that has meaningful health outcomes.

01:57:21.945 --> 01:57:23.955
Here we can address some of
those items pretty quickly.

01:57:24.615 --> 01:57:30.120
For instance, distilled water and
double distilled water is essentially

01:57:30.120 --> 01:57:34.950
distilled of that is it has magnesium
and calcium removed from it.

01:57:35.820 --> 01:57:39.600
So my recommendation would be
to not drink distilled water.

01:57:39.750 --> 01:57:44.250
There may be specific circumstances where
somebody has very high levels of blood

01:57:44.250 --> 01:57:47.940
magnesium or calcium or calcium stores
within the body that would necessitate

01:57:47.940 --> 01:57:49.530
them drinking only distilled water.

01:57:49.740 --> 01:57:52.800
But that seems like a very
isolated kind of niche case.

01:57:52.830 --> 01:57:57.000
So in general, consuming distilled
water is just simply not necessary.

01:57:57.630 --> 01:58:01.530
Now in terms of reverse osmosis
water, what is reverse osmosis water?

01:58:01.530 --> 01:58:06.540
Reverse osmosis water is water that
has been passed repeatedly through a

01:58:06.540 --> 01:58:10.770
series of filters that are designed
to remove the kinds of contaminants

01:58:10.770 --> 01:58:11.850
we were talking about earlier.

01:58:11.850 --> 01:58:17.010
So some of the basic contaminants like
disinfectant byproducts, fluoride, and

01:58:17.040 --> 01:58:21.900
some other large and small molecules
that leaves the water ideally still

01:58:21.905 --> 01:58:23.610
containing magnesium and calcium.

01:58:23.610 --> 01:58:27.030
Although there's some evidence that
reverse osmosis water can deprive water

01:58:27.030 --> 01:58:28.710
of some of the magnesium and calcium.

01:58:28.710 --> 01:58:33.030
So if you are going to use reverse
osmosis filters and drink reverse

01:58:33.030 --> 01:58:36.000
osmosis water, you want to make
sure that you're still getting the

01:58:36.005 --> 01:58:39.450
magnesium concentrations present in
that water that we talked about earlier.

01:58:40.139 --> 01:58:45.269
But in general, reverse osmosis water
is considered safe, but, and for many

01:58:45.269 --> 01:58:48.990
people, this is gonna be an important
but but very expensive to access.

01:58:49.170 --> 01:58:52.650
The reverse osmosis filters require
a lot of changing of the filters.

01:58:52.650 --> 01:58:57.030
Purchasing reverse osmosis water in
its stable form within containers,

01:58:57.030 --> 01:59:00.900
these are typically glass containers,
is going to be pretty expensive

01:59:01.139 --> 01:59:02.730
and prohibitive for most people.

01:59:03.000 --> 01:59:05.580
That said, there are a number of
people out there that really like

01:59:05.580 --> 01:59:07.530
the taste of reverse osmosis water.

01:59:08.160 --> 01:59:10.209
They report it as feeling more smooth.

01:59:11.070 --> 01:59:14.605
They think of reverse osmosis
water as "giving them energy".

01:59:15.255 --> 01:59:20.850
To be quite honest, there's no direct
studies of the subjective sensation

01:59:20.850 --> 01:59:24.610
of water in the mouth and in the
gut, and its relative health effects.

01:59:24.900 --> 01:59:29.370
Again, the smoothness of water
as one drinks it and goes down.

01:59:29.650 --> 01:59:35.980
The gut really has no direct relationship
to the "hardness or softness" of water.

01:59:36.180 --> 01:59:37.560
I know that's going to
shock a number of you.

01:59:37.560 --> 01:59:40.140
You probably think, well, hard
water is gonna be hard to drink, and

01:59:40.140 --> 01:59:41.190
it turns out that's not the case.

01:59:41.190 --> 01:59:44.760
In fact, many people find that with
elevated levels of magnesium and

01:59:44.760 --> 01:59:48.780
calcium and water, it actually tastes
smoother or softer in their mouth.

01:59:48.785 --> 01:59:51.270
So hard water tastes smooth or soft.

01:59:51.480 --> 01:59:55.650
I know it's all very counterintuitive,
but I think it's important to point this

01:59:55.650 --> 02:00:00.030
out because a number of times you'll
hear or read about filtering water so

02:00:00.030 --> 02:00:01.470
that it tastes smoother and better.

02:00:01.530 --> 02:00:05.940
And oftentimes that's happening
because the "hardness" of water that

02:00:05.945 --> 02:00:09.030
is the concentrations of magnesium
and calcium are actually increasing.

02:00:09.360 --> 02:00:13.410
So if you're somebody who's curious about
reverse osmosis water and you can afford

02:00:13.410 --> 02:00:17.910
the filters or the reverse osmosis water
already pre-filtered please be my guest.

02:00:17.915 --> 02:00:18.510
You know, drink it.

02:00:18.510 --> 02:00:20.940
I'm certainly not trying to prevent
anyone from drinking it, but there's

02:00:20.940 --> 02:00:24.480
no peer reviewed evidence that I am
aware of that conclusively shows that

02:00:24.480 --> 02:00:29.130
drinking reverse osmosis water is far
better for us than drinking other types

02:00:29.130 --> 02:00:32.340
of water, provided the other types
of water are adequately filtered of

02:00:32.340 --> 02:00:35.970
fluoride and the sorts of disinfectant
byproducts that we talked about earlier.

02:00:36.210 --> 02:00:37.560
So what about hydrogen water?

02:00:37.620 --> 02:00:40.710
You may have heard of this,
or hydrogen enriched water or

02:00:41.100 --> 02:00:46.110
electrolyzed reduced water as a way
to access hydrogen enriched water.

02:00:46.170 --> 02:00:48.180
All this might sound pretty
crazy to some of you.

02:00:48.540 --> 02:00:52.890
Now, fortunately, for sake of
today's discussion, we can take a

02:00:52.890 --> 02:00:58.170
number of the different categories
of, let's call it unique categories

02:00:58.170 --> 02:01:01.440
of water that have been described,
including deuterium-depleted water.

02:01:01.530 --> 02:01:04.110
And by the way, deuterium is
something that relates to the

02:01:04.540 --> 02:01:06.690
presence of hydrogen ions in water.

02:01:07.020 --> 02:01:12.030
And put very simply, water that is
extracted from sources that are closer

02:01:12.030 --> 02:01:17.310
to sea level tend to have more deuterium
in them than water that is extracted

02:01:17.310 --> 02:01:18.990
from sources further from sea level.

02:01:18.990 --> 02:01:23.280
So up in the mountains, for instance, and
from springs further away from oceans.

02:01:23.580 --> 02:01:27.420
As you get closer to sea level, the
sources water separate from seawater

02:01:28.320 --> 02:01:33.780
tend to have more deuterium, which
relates to the enrichment or lack

02:01:33.780 --> 02:01:37.050
of hydrogen within that water or
free hydrogen within that water.

02:01:38.670 --> 02:01:41.340
I warned you this was all gonna sound
pretty niche and that we were gonna get

02:01:41.340 --> 02:01:43.740
a little bit into the chemistry, but now
I'm gonna make it all very simple for

02:01:43.745 --> 02:01:47.250
you, at least for the non aficionado.

02:01:48.960 --> 02:01:54.870
Electrolyzed reduced water, which is
a method of using electricity to alter

02:01:54.870 --> 02:01:59.480
the confirmation of the water molecules
and their rates of movement as well,

02:02:00.350 --> 02:02:06.480
as well as so-called hydrogen rich
water, or hydrogen enriched water or

02:02:06.480 --> 02:02:12.090
deuterium-depleted water, all have the
property of having higher levels of

02:02:12.095 --> 02:02:17.040
pH than other forms of water, such as
distilled water, reverse osmosis water,

02:02:17.760 --> 02:02:21.570
and generally higher pH than the kind
of water that comes out of your tap.

02:02:21.600 --> 02:02:26.309
Unless you live in a region where
your tap water has very high levels of

02:02:26.309 --> 02:02:30.690
magnesium in it, which does occur in
certain regions of the world, but is not

02:02:30.690 --> 02:02:34.440
that common more typically, the water
that comes out of your tap does not

02:02:34.440 --> 02:02:39.540
have enough magnesium, meaning not as
much magnesium in it as you would like.

02:02:40.019 --> 02:02:44.760
And this, I believe, explains in a
fairly straightforward way why there is

02:02:44.760 --> 02:02:50.640
such an appeal of these pH enhanced or
alkaline waters or electrolyzed reduced

02:02:50.644 --> 02:02:52.740
water or deuterium-depleted water.

02:02:53.340 --> 02:02:56.370
There are a couple of reasons, but
first of all, anytime someone is

02:02:56.370 --> 02:03:00.540
consuming a specialized form of water,
chances are it's going to be filtered

02:03:00.545 --> 02:03:03.870
of the disinfectant byproducts,
fluoride, and the other things that

02:03:03.875 --> 02:03:04.860
you really don't want in water.

02:03:04.860 --> 02:03:07.050
So already the water is going
to be cleaner than would

02:03:07.055 --> 02:03:08.130
be coming out of the tap.

02:03:08.370 --> 02:03:12.660
So that's going to indirectly explain
a number of the so-called health

02:03:12.660 --> 02:03:15.960
benefits, both subjective and perhaps
even objective as we'll talk about

02:03:16.140 --> 02:03:22.140
that can result from consuming these
other let's say more esoteric forms of

02:03:22.144 --> 02:03:24.960
water, at least not of simple tap water.

02:03:26.180 --> 02:03:30.420
However, if you look at hydrogen or
hydrogen enriched water, you really need

02:03:30.424 --> 02:03:32.670
to take a step back and ask, what is that?

02:03:32.730 --> 02:03:34.080
You know, what are we
really talking about?

02:03:34.440 --> 02:03:38.580
Because it turns out that you can create
hydrogen enriched water by putting tablets

02:03:38.820 --> 02:03:43.440
of magnesium itself, small amounts of
magnesium dissolving those in water.

02:03:43.710 --> 02:03:46.040
It will give off a kind
of gaseous solution.

02:03:46.065 --> 02:03:47.280
You'll see a bunch of bubbling in there.

02:03:47.280 --> 02:03:52.139
You certainly want to dilute that
tablet and then consume the water.

02:03:52.139 --> 02:03:55.650
And yes, it's true what you've heard about
and read from these commercial sources.

02:03:55.830 --> 02:04:00.179
You do want to consume that water within
about, you know, five to 15 minutes

02:04:00.179 --> 02:04:02.880
after that tablet completes dissolving.

02:04:03.089 --> 02:04:04.220
Now, why would you do this?

02:04:04.330 --> 02:04:09.640
And I should say that I have now started
doing this not because I necessarily think

02:04:10.010 --> 02:04:13.110
that it's so necessary or so beneficial.

02:04:13.380 --> 02:04:14.639
I'll talk about my experience in a moment.

02:04:14.639 --> 02:04:18.099
I did it in anticipation of this
episode because I was researching

02:04:18.105 --> 02:04:21.030
water and hydrogen enrich water
and all these alkaline waters.

02:04:21.150 --> 02:04:25.799
And what became very clear to me
based on reading a fantastic two-part

02:04:25.799 --> 02:04:29.610
review, it's a very extensive review
entitled, or at least the first part

02:04:29.610 --> 02:04:34.799
is entitled: Electrolyzed Reduced Water
Molecular Hydrogen is the Exclusive Agent

02:04:34.799 --> 02:04:36.750
Responsible for the Therapeutic Effects.

02:04:36.755 --> 02:04:38.219
And then there's a second
part to this review.

02:04:38.370 --> 02:04:42.630
This is how extensive it is, entitled:
Electrolyzed Reduced Water number

02:04:42.630 --> 02:04:46.170
two, safety Concerns and Effectiveness
as a source of Hydrogen Water.

02:04:46.469 --> 02:04:50.730
What this review, which we've linked
to in the show notes, points to is that

02:04:51.000 --> 02:04:54.000
all of the health benefits of these
different forms of water that you hear

02:04:54.005 --> 02:04:59.325
about out there, deuterium-depleted,
hydrogen enrich, etc., all seem

02:04:59.325 --> 02:05:04.665
to boil down, no pun intended, no
boiling included, I should say, to the

02:05:04.755 --> 02:05:09.885
elevation in hydrogen that translates
into, and here's the really meaningful

02:05:09.885 --> 02:05:14.595
change, the elevation in pH that
occurs when you hydrogen enrich water.

02:05:15.075 --> 02:05:19.515
Now, there are not a lot of
clinical studies looking at hydrogen

02:05:19.515 --> 02:05:22.995
enriched water, but there are
starting to be more than a few.

02:05:23.175 --> 02:05:27.265
And one that I'd like to point out
and that we'll link to, was published

02:05:27.285 --> 02:05:31.545
fairly recently, which is entitled
Hydrogen-rich water reduces inflammatory

02:05:31.550 --> 02:05:33.465
responses and prevents apoptosis.

02:05:33.465 --> 02:05:38.115
Apoptosis is a naturally occurring cell
death during development and is generally

02:05:38.115 --> 02:05:39.855
used to describe cell death of the body.

02:05:40.245 --> 02:05:42.555
Sometimes this can be good cell
death, by the way, removing

02:05:42.585 --> 02:05:43.725
cells that need to be removed.

02:05:44.145 --> 02:05:47.295
Again, the title of the paper is:
Hydrogen-Rich water reduces inflammatory

02:05:47.715 --> 02:05:50.985
responses and prevents apoptosis of
peripheral blood cells in healthy Adults.

02:05:51.135 --> 02:05:53.415
A randomized double
blind controlled trial.

02:05:54.195 --> 02:06:01.275
Now this paper looked at the effects of
drinking 1.5 liters per day of hydrogen

02:06:01.280 --> 02:06:04.410
enriched water for a period of four weeks.

02:06:05.600 --> 02:06:11.010
They did find significant positive
benefits of reduced inflammation, and

02:06:11.010 --> 02:06:15.430
they found these changes by way of
analyzing things like interleukin 6

02:06:15.570 --> 02:06:18.300
and some of the other interleukins,
which are markers of inflammation.

02:06:18.600 --> 02:06:22.200
They controlled very nicely for the
fact that people were still consuming

02:06:22.230 --> 02:06:25.350
other forms of water and liquid and
coffee, etc., although they made

02:06:25.350 --> 02:06:28.870
sure that they weren't consuming
too much coffee and soda in addition

02:06:28.870 --> 02:06:30.630
to this hydrogen enriched water.

02:06:30.960 --> 02:06:36.330
But what this paper shows is that
indeed, increasing the free hydrogen

02:06:36.330 --> 02:06:40.320
in water can improve certain
health metrics in these cells.

02:06:40.740 --> 02:06:46.750
And this is in keeping with some of the
subjective reports that people have stated

02:06:46.770 --> 02:06:51.630
out there, and that I myself experience,
I have to say that by drinking hydrogen

02:06:51.660 --> 02:06:54.840
rich water, which I'll tell you how to
do fairly inexpensively in a moment,

02:06:55.500 --> 02:07:00.180
you do get the subjective experience of
having more energy, of "feeling better".

02:07:00.900 --> 02:07:06.110
Now, keep in mind, of course, the placebo
effect is a very real and powerful

02:07:06.115 --> 02:07:08.970
effect, so it could just be placebo,
although in this paper they did of

02:07:08.970 --> 02:07:12.195
course include a placebo group, so people
didn't know if they were getting hydrogen

02:07:12.485 --> 02:07:14.880
rich water or non hydrogen rich water.

02:07:15.090 --> 02:07:18.930
I should also mention that the
improvements in health metrics that they

02:07:18.935 --> 02:07:24.570
observed in this study were only observed
for individuals older than 30 years old.

02:07:25.110 --> 02:07:29.700
Why that is, I don't know, the conclusions
these authors came to in terms of how

02:07:30.090 --> 02:07:34.620
these individuals older than 30 achieved
lower levels, or I should say reduced

02:07:34.620 --> 02:07:39.570
levels of inflammation and improved
markers of other aspects of biological

02:07:39.570 --> 02:07:45.570
function is that the hydrogen water
improved the biological antioxidant

02:07:45.570 --> 02:07:48.420
potential of certain cell types.

02:07:48.480 --> 02:07:51.030
And again, the cell types that they
mainly focus on were these peripheral

02:07:51.035 --> 02:07:52.950
blood cells in this particular study.

02:07:53.340 --> 02:07:54.480
Now, how could this be?

02:07:54.480 --> 02:07:55.200
Why would this be?

02:07:55.200 --> 02:07:58.830
Well, this goes back to our earlier
discussion about reduction in

02:07:59.250 --> 02:08:03.450
reactive oxygen species, so-called
ROSs, and reductions in free

02:08:03.450 --> 02:08:05.460
radicals that can damage cells.

02:08:05.519 --> 02:08:09.540
So if all of this is sounding very
convoluted, I can understand why.

02:08:09.545 --> 02:08:13.110
However, what I like about this
study and the two reviews that

02:08:13.110 --> 02:08:17.160
I mentioned a moment ago is that
these studies don't really say that

02:08:17.610 --> 02:08:19.889
hydrogen-rich water is what's essential.

02:08:20.219 --> 02:08:25.650
What these studies really point to is
that the changes in pH of water that

02:08:25.710 --> 02:08:31.980
enhancing the hydrogen in water can
create, is what leads to the enhanced

02:08:32.250 --> 02:08:38.070
either absorption and or ability of
cells to utilize that higher pH water.

02:08:38.370 --> 02:08:45.210
Again, not by changing the pH of the body
or of cells, but simply because higher pH

02:08:45.210 --> 02:08:51.315
water or we could perhaps more accurately
state less acidic water, that is harder

02:08:51.315 --> 02:08:55.844
water that contains more magnesium and
calcium, seems to be more readily used

02:08:56.144 --> 02:08:59.955
by the cells of the body and therefore
it's very likely that the individuals

02:08:59.955 --> 02:09:05.175
in this study were achieving  higher
or more efficient levels of hydration.

02:09:05.445 --> 02:09:08.865
Okay, so if any of this is
confusing, let me be very clear.

02:09:09.255 --> 02:09:14.295
I do not believe that we all need to
drink deuterium-depleted water or that

02:09:14.300 --> 02:09:20.025
we all need to drink electrolyzed reduced
water, nor do I necessarily believe that

02:09:20.030 --> 02:09:22.215
we all need to drink hydrogen rich water.

02:09:22.335 --> 02:09:27.585
However, it's very clear to me that
all these different forms of water are

02:09:27.585 --> 02:09:32.415
better absorbed and therefore lead to
better and more efficient hydration, and

02:09:32.415 --> 02:09:36.945
therefore can reduce inflammation, blood
pressure, and improve a number of other

02:09:36.945 --> 02:09:42.554
health metrics because of the elevated pH
that all of these different purification

02:09:42.554 --> 02:09:44.804
or water treatment methods achieve.

02:09:44.985 --> 02:09:48.554
And that elevated pH, again, is not
changing the pH of the cells and

02:09:48.554 --> 02:09:49.844
tissues and organs of your body.

02:09:49.844 --> 02:09:54.764
You actually don't want that, rather that
elevated pH is simply making the water

02:09:54.764 --> 02:09:57.105
less acidic than it would be otherwise.

02:09:57.405 --> 02:10:01.425
So the simple takeaway is this, if
your tap water contains sufficient

02:10:01.425 --> 02:10:05.715
magnesium per the values that we
talked about earlier, I don't think

02:10:05.715 --> 02:10:07.545
you need to hydrogen enrich your water.

02:10:07.665 --> 02:10:13.095
I do however, suggest that you at least
analyze your water or look at some of

02:10:13.095 --> 02:10:19.575
the professional analysis of water that
you can achieve online and filter out

02:10:19.995 --> 02:10:25.365
disinfectant byproducts and fluorides,
etc., from that magnesium, or I should say

02:10:25.370 --> 02:10:27.285
sufficiently magnesium containing water.

02:10:27.465 --> 02:10:27.795
Okay?

02:10:27.795 --> 02:10:31.755
Put simply, if your tap water has
enough magnesium, filter it, but drink

02:10:31.755 --> 02:10:33.525
it and I think you're doing just fine.

02:10:34.035 --> 02:10:39.135
If, however, the levels of magnesium in
your tap water are not above that value

02:10:39.135 --> 02:10:44.655
that we talked about earlier in that
case, I do think, and I can completely

02:10:44.660 --> 02:10:49.365
understand why enriching the amount of
hydrogen in that water can make that

02:10:49.365 --> 02:10:52.495
water not only more palatable, right?

02:10:52.935 --> 02:10:57.435
Give you the sensation that it's
softer or smoother or more enjoyable to

02:10:57.435 --> 02:10:59.955
drink than more acidic water would be.

02:11:00.165 --> 02:11:04.305
But also that that water is going
to be far more effective in being

02:11:04.305 --> 02:11:07.635
absorbed and hydrating in the cells and
tissues of your body, which turns out

02:11:07.640 --> 02:11:11.535
to be very important for an enormous
range, perhaps every biological

02:11:11.895 --> 02:11:13.155
function within your brain and body.

02:11:13.755 --> 02:11:16.815
So how can you hydrogen enrich your water?

02:11:16.995 --> 02:11:19.895
That actually can be done
fairly inexpensively.

02:11:20.025 --> 02:11:23.365
I've been doing that as I mentioned
earlier, as part of an experiment in

02:11:23.365 --> 02:11:26.085
preparation for this episode, because
it turns out that the water that comes

02:11:26.090 --> 02:11:30.405
out of my tap has very little magnesium
in it and very little calcium as well.

02:11:31.650 --> 02:11:35.670
The way to create hydrogen-rich water
is you can simply purchase molecular

02:11:35.670 --> 02:11:40.470
hydrogen tablets, which in reality are
just magnesium tablets that dissolve in

02:11:40.470 --> 02:11:45.269
water and create a free hydrogen that can
interact with the other water molecules.

02:11:45.660 --> 02:11:49.110
Now, the chemistry behind it has
been substantiated, and I'll provide

02:11:49.170 --> 02:11:52.950
a link in the show note captions to
a paper that gets into some fairly

02:11:52.950 --> 02:11:57.269
extensive detail about the way that
having an additional hydrogen in your

02:11:57.269 --> 02:12:02.160
water can adjust the flow of electrons
and the adjustment of free radicals.

02:12:02.250 --> 02:12:06.269
But keep in mind, again, this is all
through increases in the pH of your water,

02:12:06.540 --> 02:12:11.370
and please keep in mind that you can't
simply take any other or any old magnesium

02:12:11.370 --> 02:12:14.099
tablet or capsule and put it into water.

02:12:14.340 --> 02:12:18.540
The configuration of the magnesium
in these capsules and tablets is such

02:12:18.540 --> 02:12:23.509
that it allows a rapid dissolving
of the tablet and the activation

02:12:23.509 --> 02:12:26.389
of the free hydrogen that can
interact with the water molecules.

02:12:26.629 --> 02:12:29.570
Again, there are only a few
scientific studies exploring

02:12:29.870 --> 02:12:34.029
the real biological effects of
these activated hydrogen waters.

02:12:34.549 --> 02:12:39.884
The dissolvable tablets are the far
less expensive way to go than purchasing

02:12:40.215 --> 02:12:42.710
pre-packaged and sealed hydrogen water.

02:12:42.919 --> 02:12:48.169
In fact, I don't recommend those brands
because they are quite expensive and

02:12:48.169 --> 02:12:53.210
it's not clear how stable the activated
or free hydrogen is in those waters.

02:12:53.509 --> 02:12:57.349
In any case, this is certainly not
something that everyone needs to do.

02:12:57.500 --> 02:13:01.099
I mention it because I have had
a good experience with it myself.

02:13:01.190 --> 02:13:05.389
I also will mention again that I
have no business or affiliation

02:13:05.389 --> 02:13:06.320
to any of these products.

02:13:06.320 --> 02:13:08.870
I'll provide a link to a few of them
in the show note captions for those

02:13:08.875 --> 02:13:10.250
of you that want to experiment.

02:13:10.254 --> 02:13:12.379
And indeed, that's why I'm telling
you this, for those of you that want

02:13:12.379 --> 02:13:16.940
to experiment with raising the pH of
your water without having to purchase

02:13:17.179 --> 02:13:21.679
what is ordinarily quite expensive,
higher pH water, you can do this with

02:13:21.679 --> 02:13:23.509
these dissolvable magnesium tablet.

02:13:23.835 --> 02:13:25.844
My experience with them
has been quite good.

02:13:26.264 --> 02:13:29.835
In fact, I plan to continue to
use them once or twice a day.

02:13:29.835 --> 02:13:32.775
This is not the sort of thing
that you need to do in all

02:13:32.775 --> 02:13:33.674
the water that you drink.

02:13:33.674 --> 02:13:37.004
I want to repeat, even if you go down
this path and you find that you really

02:13:37.004 --> 02:13:41.415
like the activated hydrogen tablet
approach, it is not the case that you

02:13:41.415 --> 02:13:44.655
want to put these in all of your water,
and you certainly don't want to put

02:13:44.655 --> 02:13:46.964
them in carbonated waters of any kind.

02:13:47.294 --> 02:13:50.294
That will lead to a lot of gastric
discomfort, nor do you want to put

02:13:50.294 --> 02:13:52.304
them into hot liquids of any kind.

02:13:52.304 --> 02:13:55.995
So again, this is the sort of thing
that you do once or twice, maybe three

02:13:56.000 --> 02:14:00.674
times a day, and you can find out for
yourself and sort of measure subjectively

02:14:00.705 --> 02:14:04.554
whether or not you like the experience
and whether or not you "feel better".

02:14:04.865 --> 02:14:08.115
Now, earlier in the episode we
were discussing structured water

02:14:08.265 --> 02:14:10.005
or this fourth phase of water.

02:14:10.485 --> 02:14:13.995
I know a number of people out there are
curious as to whether or not ingesting

02:14:14.405 --> 02:14:20.055
structured water is somehow better for
us than ingesting non-structured water.

02:14:20.655 --> 02:14:25.485
All I can say about this is that it is
a very controversial thing to suggest

02:14:25.485 --> 02:14:29.745
that structured water is somehow
more biologically effective or better

02:14:29.745 --> 02:14:31.875
for us than non-structured water.

02:14:32.325 --> 02:14:35.755
There are a number of different ways
that one can create structured water.

02:14:36.285 --> 02:14:41.724
They involve some pretty extensive and
expensive at-home systems ranging anywhere

02:14:41.745 --> 02:14:44.894
from a couple of hundred dollars to
a couple of thousand dollars or more.

02:14:45.435 --> 02:14:49.455
To be quite direct, when one goes into
the peer reviewed scientific literature,

02:14:49.785 --> 02:14:55.345
one will not find that is there is
essentially no real evidence that

02:14:55.345 --> 02:15:00.955
ingesting structured water leads to any
specific desired biological outcomes.

02:15:01.405 --> 02:15:04.465
Now, as I say that, I'm sure there
are people out there who have still

02:15:04.465 --> 02:15:08.695
had tremendous experiences ingesting
structured water, whether or not that's

02:15:08.700 --> 02:15:12.745
due to a placebo effect or a real effect
of ingesting structured water isn't clear.

02:15:13.345 --> 02:15:16.345
Just to give you a sense of what my
stance is on things like structured

02:15:16.345 --> 02:15:20.365
water, I think that they are interesting
and intriguing, but as a scientist, in

02:15:20.365 --> 02:15:24.835
the absence of any quality peer review
data at present, I can't really suggest

02:15:24.835 --> 02:15:29.965
that people go out and start ingesting
structured water nor that they adhere

02:15:29.965 --> 02:15:33.655
to the claims that structured water
is going to be really, really good for

02:15:33.655 --> 02:15:35.245
them compared to other forms of water.

02:15:35.305 --> 02:15:39.235
That said, I do think that there's
an interesting and open space for

02:15:39.240 --> 02:15:43.525
further exploration of the biological
effects of structured water given the

02:15:43.530 --> 02:15:45.775
fact that structured water does exist.

02:15:45.780 --> 02:15:48.835
I don't think anyone debates that,
and the fact that the different

02:15:48.835 --> 02:15:51.805
structures of water in this fourth
phase of water as we're calling it,

02:15:52.225 --> 02:15:58.025
has been shown to interface with solids
and other aspects of liquids and can

02:15:58.025 --> 02:16:00.245
do so within organelles of cells.

02:16:00.545 --> 02:16:02.975
So different components of
cells that control different

02:16:02.975 --> 02:16:04.445
functions, including mitochondria.

02:16:04.685 --> 02:16:07.685
I think there's a potential there,
whether or not there's a promise

02:16:07.685 --> 02:16:10.325
there, is a another question entirely.

02:16:10.625 --> 02:16:13.025
So I don't wanna shut the
door on structured water.

02:16:13.205 --> 02:16:16.355
I think this is an open question
that I hope there will be more

02:16:16.355 --> 02:16:20.105
data to answer those questions
in the not too distant future.

02:16:20.285 --> 02:16:24.215
And meanwhile, if any of you are aware
of good clinical studies exploring

02:16:24.455 --> 02:16:28.145
the biological effects of structured
water in either animal models or

02:16:28.145 --> 02:16:32.555
humans, please put those references
in the comments on YouTube because I'm

02:16:32.559 --> 02:16:36.605
very curious as to how this area of
biological effects of structured water

02:16:36.875 --> 02:16:38.855
is evolving and continues to evolve.

02:16:39.335 --> 02:16:43.055
So today we discussed water, and
admittedly we went into a lot of

02:16:43.055 --> 02:16:46.955
detail about the physics and chemistry
of water in its various forms.

02:16:47.225 --> 02:16:50.345
And we talked about hydration because
I think that's the main reason

02:16:50.345 --> 02:16:53.764
why many of you are interested
in or concerned about water.

02:16:54.095 --> 02:16:56.885
We also talked about contaminants
and tap water, which unfortunately

02:16:57.215 --> 02:17:01.775
do exist and are very prominent in
essentially all regions of the world.

02:17:01.805 --> 02:17:04.985
So please do get some information
about what's coming out of your tap.

02:17:05.195 --> 02:17:09.005
I also wanna throw in one other piece of
information that's really critical that

02:17:09.005 --> 02:17:13.055
I learned about when researching this
episode, which is the quality of water

02:17:13.055 --> 02:17:16.625
that comes out of your tap is not just
dictated by the source that it comes

02:17:16.625 --> 02:17:22.065
from external to your home or apartment,
your pipes are also important, and that

02:17:22.065 --> 02:17:28.005
filter, or that little mesh that sits at
the faucet head is also very important.

02:17:28.065 --> 02:17:31.155
Most people don't pay attention to that,
but it turns out that a lot of debris

02:17:31.155 --> 02:17:37.845
and contaminants can be derived from
that little filter that most people just

02:17:37.845 --> 02:17:39.825
simply aren't cleaning often enough.

02:17:39.855 --> 02:17:44.685
So here, I'm not trying to tell you
that the metal or the plastic that

02:17:44.685 --> 02:17:46.425
that filter is made of is a problem.

02:17:46.785 --> 02:17:50.775
More often than not, contaminants are
showing up in water because people aren't

02:17:50.775 --> 02:17:52.965
cleaning those filters often enough.

02:17:52.965 --> 02:17:55.995
And in fact, prior to researching
this episode, I didn't ever

02:17:56.015 --> 02:17:57.135
think to clean that filter.

02:17:57.525 --> 02:18:02.325
I looked underneath my faucet and while
that filter didn't look particularly

02:18:02.325 --> 02:18:05.865
filled with debris, I did find that when
I took it off and I looked at the other

02:18:05.865 --> 02:18:07.905
sign, there was quite a lot of debris.

02:18:07.935 --> 02:18:10.575
So if you are going to consume tap
water, you definitely want to consider

02:18:10.575 --> 02:18:14.685
the source, the pipes in your building
or apartment, the ones that lead right

02:18:14.685 --> 02:18:19.440
up to your glass or jug that you would
put that water into, and also that

02:18:19.440 --> 02:18:23.610
mesh that that water passes through
as it goes into that glass or jug.

02:18:24.000 --> 02:18:26.160
We also talked about
how much water to drink.

02:18:26.610 --> 02:18:28.980
I hope that we finally
resolve that question.

02:18:28.980 --> 02:18:31.080
For those of you that have
been wondering about that.

02:18:31.085 --> 02:18:34.650
The Galpin equation is a wonderful
approach to how much water

02:18:34.655 --> 02:18:36.370
to consume during exercise.

02:18:36.660 --> 02:18:41.590
And by providing these other formulas
of about 8 ounces or 240 milliliters

02:18:41.615 --> 02:18:46.920
of water per hour for the 10 hours
from waking until post waking on

02:18:46.920 --> 02:18:48.150
average, remember it's averages.

02:18:48.150 --> 02:18:51.410
You don't have to consume them every hour
on the hour, and no need to be neurotic.

02:18:51.789 --> 02:18:55.590
Hopefully you can achieve better
levels of hydration, which we know can

02:18:55.590 --> 02:19:00.450
lead to reductions in blood pressure
improvements in appetite, mood, and focus.

02:19:00.450 --> 02:19:04.950
And I really think that it's the
improvements in cognitive focus and

02:19:05.889 --> 02:19:10.089
physical ability, both endurance strength
and other forms of kind of readiness

02:19:10.110 --> 02:19:13.590
in the body, readiness to perform
work in the body that really are best

02:19:13.590 --> 02:19:15.299
supported by the hydration literature.

02:19:15.690 --> 02:19:18.719
And then of course, we went through the
different forms of water that you hear

02:19:18.725 --> 02:19:22.920
about out there and addressed which ones
are going to be beneficial or not and

02:19:22.920 --> 02:19:27.330
perhaps more importantly, why any of
them  would be beneficial thinking about

02:19:27.334 --> 02:19:31.799
that from the perspective of biologists
and the chemistry of water, and I do

02:19:31.799 --> 02:19:35.549
hope that by arriving at this point in
the episode, now that you have a much

02:19:35.549 --> 02:19:39.330
better understanding of the chemistry
and physics of water and the way that

02:19:39.330 --> 02:19:41.670
water can powerfully impact your biology.

